# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Named explicitly rather than relying on a blanket `*.json`. The repo is
# PUBLIC, so this list is the last line of defence — add to it, never remove.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!*.env.example
key.json
**/key.json
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
*-sa.json
*.pem
*.p12
*.key

# ── User finance data (privacy, not secrecy) ─────────────────────────────────
# These hold real expense/income records. Never commit them.
data.json
rules.json
**/data.json
backups/

# ── Local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.streamlit/secrets.toml
licenses.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── Node / web ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
web/dist/
.vercel

# NOTE: `*.json` used to be ignored wholesale. That also excluded
# web/package.json, web/package-lock.json and web/vercel.json — without which
# the Vercel build of web/ cannot run at all — while giving only incidental
# cover to the real secrets, which are now listed above by name.
